      "rev_n_1_0e9b07_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_0e9b07_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_0e9b07",
        "thought_text": "Instead of checking if the total sum is odd, a better approach would be to focus on the parity of the sum of the first n elements. If the sum of the first n elements is odd, we can always find a way to reorder the array to make the sums unequal. This is because we can always move an odd number to the second half or an even number to the first half, ensuring that the parity of the sums changes.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_0e9b07_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_2fc7642483",
        "created_at": 1794529790.4451358
      },
      "rev_n_3_5d9a6b_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_5d9a6b_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_5d9a6b",
        "thought_text": "Instead of using a greedy approach to pair the largest element with the smallest element, consider using a more systematic approach that considers all possible ways to partition the array into two groups of equal size. This approach would involve iterating through all possible combinations of elements for the first group and checking if the remaining elements form the second group with a different sum.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_5d9a6b_0",
